---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '../lib/site.js';

const host = SITE.domain.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms governing your use of RigFloorHQ, including the limits of our educational content, the well control calculators, and liability."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Terms of Service', href: '/terms' }]}
  lang="en"
  alternateHref="/es/terms"
>
  <Nav slot="nav" lang="en" alternateHref="/es/terms" />
  <Footer slot="footer" lang="en" />

  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero-eyebrow">Legal</div>
    <h1>Terms of <span>Service</span></h1>
    <p class="page-hero-sub">The agreement between you and us — and, more importantly, the limits of what this site is for.</p>
    <div class="page-meta">
      <span class="page-meta-item">Last updated <strong>{LEGAL.lastUpdated}</strong></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>About these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are an agreement between you and <strong>{LEGAL.legalName}</strong>{LEGAL.address ? `, ${LEGAL.address}` : ''}
        ("we", "us"), and govern your use of {host} (the "Service"). By using the Service
        you accept them. If you do not accept them, please do not use the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>Reference material, not operational instruction</h2>
      <div class="danger-box">
        <strong>Read this section before using anything on this site at work.</strong>
        {SITE.name} publishes educational and reference material about drilling, well
        control, rig equipment, welding and oilfield careers. It is <strong>not</strong> an
        operating procedure, a well plan, a training qualification, or a substitute for
        any of them. Nothing here authorises, approves or certifies any action on a rig.
      </div>
      <p>
        Well control and rig floor work are safety-critical. Decisions must be made under
        your employer's approved procedures, the applicable regulatory requirements, the
        specific well programme, and the direction of your certified well control
        supervisor and competent supervision on site. Where anything on this site differs
        from those, <strong>those govern and this site does not</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reading this site does not make anyone competent to perform a task. Formal
        competence comes from accredited training and assessment — for example IWCF or IADC
        WellSharp certification for well control — together with supervised experience.
        We do not assess anyone, and we issue no certification of any kind.
      </p>

      <h2>The calculators</h2>
      <p>
        The Service includes calculators covering hydrostatic pressure, kill sheets and mud
        weight windows. They exist so people can learn how the arithmetic works and check
        their understanding while studying. They run in your browser, we never see what you
        enter, and we never see what they output.
      </p>
      <div class="danger-box">
        <strong>Do not use these calculators to make decisions on a live well.</strong>
        They are unverified teaching tools. They use simplified assumptions, they do not
        know your well, your fluid, your equipment or your conditions, and their output is
        not checked by anyone. Use the kill sheet and calculation methods approved by your
        operator, verified by your well control supervisor.
      </div>
      <p>
        Any figure produced by a calculator on this site is an illustration. You are
        responsible for verifying every number you rely on, by an approved method.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and currency</h2>
      <p>
        We take care to describe standards, practices and equipment accurately, but
        standards are revised, regulations change and practice varies between operators,
        contractors and jurisdictions. Where we reference a standard or regulation, always
        work from the current published version rather than our summary of it. We do not
        warrant that any part of the Service is complete, current or free from error.
      </p>
      <p>
        Career, pay and certification information is general and indicative. Rates and
        requirements vary by region, employer, contract and market conditions.
      </p>

      <h2>Translations</h2>
      <p>
        Much of the Service, including these terms, is published in Spanish for
        convenience. The English version is the original. Where a translation and the
        English differ in meaning, <strong>the English version prevails</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your use of our content</h2>
      <p>
        The content on this Service was researched, written, compiled and arranged by us,
        and is protected by copyright and other intellectual property laws. We provide it
        for your personal, non-commercial use.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may not use, or authorise anyone else to use, the Service or its content in any
        manner that acts as a substitute for it, competes with it, or affects our ability to
        operate it. These restrictions apply equally to robots, spiders, scrapers, crawlers,
        automated collection of any kind, and to the bulk reproduction of our material for
        training or republication. You agree not to bypass measures used to limit automated
        access, and to respect the directives in our
        <a href="/robots.txt">robots.txt</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may quote short extracts for comment, review, teaching or news reporting,
        provided you credit {SITE.name} and link to the page you took them from. If you want
        to use something more substantially — in a training pack, for instance — email us
        and we will usually say yes.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        The Service links to third-party sites, standards bodies and training providers. We
        do not control them, we are not responsible for their content or accuracy, and a
        link is not an endorsement. Following an external link is at your own risk.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We provide the Service on an "as is" and "as available" basis. We do not guarantee
        it will be uninterrupted, error-free or continuously available, and we may change,
        suspend or discontinue any part of it at any time without notice.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we exclude all warranties, express or
        implied, as to the accuracy, completeness or fitness for purpose of the Service and
        its content.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss, damage,
        injury or cost arising from your use of, or reliance on, the Service — including
        any operational decision, any calculation, any well control action, any equipment
        or procedure choice, and any career or financial decision. Reliance on this
        material in an operational setting is at your own risk and, where you are at work,
        remains subject to your employer's procedures and supervision.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability where it would be unlawful to do
        so, including for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or for fraud. Some
        jurisdictions do not allow certain exclusions, so parts of this section may not
        apply to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what we collect — very little —
        and our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> explains why there is no cookie banner.
        Both form part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The current version is always the one
        published on this page, with the date shown above. Continuing to use the Service
        after a change means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of {LEGAL.governingLaw}, and the courts of
        {LEGAL.governingLaw} have jurisdiction over any dispute. If you are a consumer, this
        does not deprive you of the protection of any mandatory consumer rights available
        under the law of the country where you live.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms:
        <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contactEmail}`}>{LEGAL.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
